#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436139} :activity/id #uuid "a554ac31-b397-5970-b942-0ac30a77ef87" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048315 :topic/id #uuid "93e6a7ce-2e63-5dea-bbbb-a00575db5770" :topic/math-academy-id 1852} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436139 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436132} {:answer/id #uuid "94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436133} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436134} {:answer/id #uuid "a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436135} {:answer/id #uuid "caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436132} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4437cfd-d611-50b5-a26a-25a34c0f8218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813" :question/math-academy-id "q-34636" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-2.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-2\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436142}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436140 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ea0212-0c8f-50de-a9e9-986f267bdb5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339138} {:answer/id #uuid "25b09d72-beeb-56f8-b3c5-bd45509568ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339451} {:answer/id #uuid "392acaa5-a047-5743-bd68-0e133d8bead9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339642} {:answer/id #uuid "c4734975-ddc9-5119-b9e9-59e873e223ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340873} {:answer/id #uuid "d55e6034-4f45-5b74-b206-75e90bc1aef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341016}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339138} :answer-field/id #uuid "690b25a1-892c-577b-b6f7-6ff437d6dcd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e12a2efc-9d88-56c5-96b5-ec530d76269d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74594" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436141}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436141 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285f60c4-cfc6-509d-a8ca-df316a92348e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238408} {:answer/id #uuid "306f3ae9-9703-5c61-9e1f-a029efeb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238477} {:answer/id #uuid "7197f81b-8003-5f00-b98f-69a60e60b685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239030} {:answer/id #uuid "7aef6609-8c36-5411-ba86-81d4a40f69b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239115} {:answer/id #uuid "db09174f-1cdc-5bdb-8120-63756b097fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239966} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5dbe15-3666-592c-9f7a-5c21bff9ad15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "edff4129-bf9d-5206-854e-d3e5b43ca237" :question/math-academy-id "q-105253" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩$, $c=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-5,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ 3s-t=-5 \\\\ 2s-t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"} :step/id #uuid "70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436143}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436142 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28049f08-5684-5304-ad3d-9f534b59f279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339478} {:answer/id #uuid "67519cd7-cc6e-5952-bf35-4a4a24da747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} {:answer/id #uuid "79c14b9a-0376-5405-a220-fdac02f464da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340214} {:answer/id #uuid "92c70a7d-6a91-5cb6-8d17-c5ff99a5580f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340448} {:answer/id #uuid "b383d39f-e410-5314-b906-611aa1b45702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340043} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c41871-59a4-56ef-80fe-7d004904e3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "62066547-f160-5da7-be83-cd71028d6d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-74556" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436140}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436143 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145063fc-8e8e-5c5e-b9c0-4ce50643aeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238221} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd14ba1-3c05-5721-9490-57e8bf80fea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} {:answer/id #uuid "a01540c4-5818-561d-9151-d28aeb0e7fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239452} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e4047e-41ea-50d0-ab94-58e7363cb874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239637} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdd9058-9132-5515-90b7-33b231320d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238742} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dee8bc9-1a1f-59f0-8b66-162d23f34c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8c4cb4f7-2d57-5ca9-8ffa-a4fe4548b0de" :question/math-academy-id "q-105265" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,-1,4⟩$, $c=⟨-3,-8,14⟩$, and  $u=⟨5,-10,-14⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ -s-8t=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ t=3 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-14b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$"} :step/id #uuid "acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f4636"}] :activity/title "Linear Span of Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436131}]}
